---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LayeredArchitectureGraphic from '../../components/LayeredArchitectureGraphic.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Platform Convergence Playbook — North End Technology"
  description="Collapse fragmented product silos onto one shared infrastructure layer."
>
  <section class="playbook-hero section-alt">
    <div class="wrapper">
      <p class="eyebrow">Playbook</p>
      <h1>Platform Convergence</h1>
      <p>
        The playbook every other playbook on this site depends on: collapsing
        fragmented product silos onto a single, shared platform infrastructure.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrapper">
      <LayeredArchitectureGraphic class="convergence-graphic" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-alt">
    <div class="wrapper playbook-body">
      <h2>The joint-planning gauntlet</h2>
      <p>
        Convergence fails when it's treated as an architecture diagram instead of a
        planning exercise. It succeeds when every product manager and engineering
        lead who owns a silo sits through the same joint-planning gauntlet and leaves
        with a shared roadmap.
      </p>

      <h2>The convergence sequence</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Map every silo's dependency surface first.</strong> You cannot converge what you haven't fully inventoried — undocumented integrations are where convergence timelines die.</li>
        <li><strong>Run joint planning as one gauntlet, not sequential meetings.</strong> Put every silo's product and engineering leadership in the same planning cycle so trade-offs are negotiated once, in the open, not renegotiated per team.</li>
        <li><strong>Design the shared layer for the laggard, not the leader.</strong> The platform's first version should absorb the least mature silo's requirements — it's the one most likely to resist migration otherwise.</li>
        <li><strong>Migrate on a forcing function.</strong> A shared platform without a decommission date for the old systems becomes a permanent second system to maintain.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why this is the foundation playbook</h2>
      <p>
        EBITDA defense, AI monetization, and NRR acceleration all assume a platform
        capable of supporting them. Convergence is the prerequisite work — the layer
        every other initiative is built on top of.
      </p>

      <div class="playbook-cta">
        <a href={`${base}/#contact`} class="btn btn-primary">Discuss this playbook</a>
        <a href={`${base}/#playbooks`} class="back-link">&larr; Back to all playbooks</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .convergence-graphic {
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
</style>
